## To Alice: two things I added beyond the letter of the brief

- **When a discussion is closed.** The join prompt used to say "if none has
  today's date, the observer creates it". With numbers that test no longer
  works, since two discussions can open on one day. I wrote: if the folder
  with the highest number already holds a `consolidation.hmd`, the discussion
  is closed and the observer opens the next. Say if you want another test.
- **Two discussions on one day.** The rules now say that the number, not the
  date, tells discussions apart and orders them. SLH-D-0001 and SLH-D-0002
  are the case.

